@title STORY • NOAH: NICOLE'S BIG BROTHER
@bg dorm_room_day
You're Noah Miller. Distance runner. Professionally chill. Your phone has 47 texts from your little sister Nicole, the soccer captain, and it's 9 a.m.
Nicole: "valentina is talking to marco AGAIN"
Nicole: "who is marco you ask. a shortstop. a SHORTSTOP noah"
Nicole: "answer me"
> [Sweet] Call her. -> a1
> [Good] "who is marco" -> a2
> [Bold] "nic it's 9am. i'm a distance runner. i have one emotion and it's tired" -> a3
*a1
@add Nicole_Bond 3
She talks for twenty-two minutes. You say "mm" eleven times. At the end she says "thanks for always listening." You realize you'd do it a thousand more times.
@jump a_done
*a2
Nicole: "THAT'S WHAT I SAID"
You've accidentally said the right thing. You'll take it.
@jump a_done
*a3
@add Nicole_Bond 1
Nicole: "rude. love you. go run"
*a_done
@bg trail_morning
@show logan
Long run with Logan. Ten miles. He says four words total. It's your favorite part of the week.
Logan: (mile seven) You okay?
Noah: Why?
Logan: You're running fast. You only run fast when you're thinking.
> [Good] "Nicole's whole team is falling apart and she thinks it's her fault." -> b1
> [Sweet] "I miss home. Denver. Mountains. My mom's breakfast burritos." -> b2
> [Bold] "I'm thinking about transferring." -> b3
*b1
@add Logan_Bond 2
Logan: (after a whole mile) You can't fix it for her. You can just be there when it breaks.
Noah: When did you get so wise?
Logan: I read.
@jump end
*b2
@add Logan_Bond 2
Logan: (stopping on the trail) There's a mountain view three miles that way. Want to see it?
You run an extra six miles. Totally worth it.
@jump end
*b3
@add Logan_Bond 3
Logan stops running completely. He's never stopped running in the middle of a long run.
Logan: Don't.
That's the most emotional thing he's ever said. You don't transfer.
*end
Noah Miller acts like nothing bothers him. Really, he just carries his worry quietly, in the background, like a long, easy run.
